1. Component Function Pehli Baar Chalta Hai
React aapke component function ko top se bottom tak execute karta hai.
useState apne initial value ke sath memory mein state variable banata hai.

2. Pehla Virtual DOM Banta Hai
Function return hone wale JSX ko process karta hai aur ek initial Virtual DOM tree (memory mein ek blueprint) tayar karta hai.

3. Real DOM mein Insertion (Mounting / Paint)
React is Virtual DOM ko real browser DOM mein inject kar deta hai.

Iske baad hi woh element ya page aapko browser screen par nazar (render) aata hai.

4. useEffect Hooks Run Hote hain
Jab component screen par completely mount ho jata hai, tab agar koi useEffect laga ho toh woh execute hota hai.
Agar dependency array empty [] ho, toh yeh sirf pehli baar (on mount) hi chalta hai (jaise APIs se data fetch karne ya timers lagane ke liye).

1-Line Answer (Short Summary):
"Initial render (Mounting) mein component execute ho kar initial state ke sath pehla Virtual DOM banata hai, usay Real DOM mein mount karta hai, aur phir useEffect run karta hai."

